TIP:  Okay, so in the original Bobby recorded the third verse a semi-tone higher than the previous ones which just makes everything unnecessarily messy and all those sharped chords are not presented here.  But, if you want to play it as originally recorded move the capo up one fret.  Or if you don't care to match the recording you can jump down to the -------- and play the rest of the song up a full semi-tone.  Or still, the simplest option, you can simply ignore the (Capo) and play the rest of the song just as you did the first part, in (C) and stop before the key change.  
 
      
